// #80 FOLLOW-UP — THE PLACE-SLOT DECLINES, EXECUTED.
//
// `MLIRGenImpl::place_slot_type` decides the byte size of a PLACE: an array /
// Vec element stride, a GEP into an aggregate, and — since #80 — the slot of a
// deferred `let v: T;`. It had two arms that GUESSED instead of declining:
//
//   * a NULL TypeRef answered `i32` — a FOUR-byte place, smaller than every
//     fat repr and than most scalars, so the stride/GEP/slot built from it is
//     wrong in the direction that overwrites the neighbour;
//   * a Struct whose `mlir_struct_key` misses `struct_types_` (the open
//     bare-name class #58/#60/#61) answered the 8-byte HANDLE `ptr` — a place
//     type for a struct of any size, and #80 made it a deferred-`let` slot
//     that `var_struct_` then memcpy's the struct's real footprint into.
//
// Both are now reported on the `bug` channel ⇒ COMPILE FAILED, no object file.
//
// NEITHER FIRES ANYWHERE IN THE TREE. That is the point and the problem: the
// state they name is a compiler malfunction, so correct codegen cannot reach
// them, and a report no program executes is a green nobody ran (exactly what
// `check_slot_fits` was caught being — `fail/mlirgen_slot_fits_sensor`). The
// measurement is self-instrumenting rather than a fire counter that can go
// stale: the sink FAILS THE COMPILE, so the green stdlib+examples build and the
// green fixture corpus could not be hiding a fire.
//
// THIS FILE PINS THE SECOND ONE. It executes the struct-key-miss arm through
// the name-scoped fault injection in `declare_local_place`: a local named
// `__slotmiss_canary*` asks `place_slot_type` with `slot_decline_canary_` set,
// which forces the `struct_types_` lookup to take its miss arm. The NULL arm
// has its own fixture, `fail/mlirgen_place_slot_null_decline` — ONE PREFIX PER
// ARM, because the fail runner greps the whole `.expected` as a FIXED pattern
// and a two-line expectation is an OR, so one file asserting both texts would
// stay green after either report was deleted. Delete this decline, or the
// injection, and this file goes green-by-silence — logosc succeeds, stderr
// carries nothing, and the fail runner reds it.
//
// THE ADMIT HALF OF THE PAIR: `pass/bc_fatval_deferred_init_len` cell 14/15 is
// the same `let st: W;` declaration with an ordinary name — it compiles, and
// the struct lands in its real 24-byte slot.
package mlirgen_place_slot_decline;

pub struct W { pub s: str, pub n: i64 }

unsafe fn main() -> i32 {
    let __slotmiss_canary_st: W;
    __slotmiss_canary_st = W { s: "abcde", n: 9i64 };
    if __slotmiss_canary_st.n != 9i64 { return 1; }
    return 0;
}
